x86_64-linux  cxx1 emits the C1 form of each class's implicit default constructor beside the C2 where clang emits only the C2 a use asks for. The difference implicit-move.nonames records, and inescapable here because these are the constructors the *compiler* writes - the whole point of the case is that they are written at all, Base's default constructor being protected - and one is inline by nature with no out-of-line form to switch to. C1 and C2 are identical for a class with no virtual bases and both are mergeable, so the extra costs object size and nothing else. x86_64-windows agrees on all 11 names.
arm64-darwin  the same C1 forms, the two Itanium targets emitting these the same way as each other.
